# The app owns /wiki/<title>; everything else must resolve to a real file.
#
# Cloudflare Pages otherwise answers any unmatched path with index.html and a 200,
# including a missing /assets/… file. Combined with the year-long immutable cache
# in _headers, one request during a deploy window pinned index.html into the cache
# entry for a stylesheet URL and served the whole site unstyled — twice, once per
# cache variant. With this rewrite plus 404.html, a missing asset is a 404 that
# nothing will mistake for CSS, and deep links still open the reader.
/wiki/* /index.html 200
